### Expected behavior
Handler should be really removed from the pipeline when they add failed.
### Actual behavior
Handler is not removed from the pipeline although the handlerState is 'REMOVE_COMPLETE' 
### Minimal yet complete reproducer code (or URL to code)
```java
public class ChannelPipelineTest {

    @Test
    public void testAddHandlerFailed() throws InterruptedException {
        EventLoop eventLoop = new NioEventLoopGroup(1).next();
        EventExecutorGroup group = new DefaultEventExecutorGroup(16);
        final int handlerSize = 32;
        try {
            Channel channel = new NioServerSocketChannel();
            channel.config().setOption(ChannelOption.SINGLE_EVENTEXECUTOR_PER_GROUP, false);
            channel.pipeline().addFirst(new NoopChannelHandler());

            List<ChannelHandlerContext> ctxList = new ArrayList<>(handlerSize);
            for (int i = 0; i < handlerSize; i++) {
                channel.pipeline().addFirst(group, i + "", new BadChannelHandler());
                ctxList.add(channel.pipeline().context(i + ""));
            }
            eventLoop.register(channel).sync();

            for (int i = 0; i < handlerSize; i++) {
                while (!ctxList.get(i).isRemoved()) {
                    eventLoop.awaitTermination(100, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
                }
                assertThat(channel.pipeline().context(i + "")).isNull();
            }
        } finally {
            eventLoop.shutdownGracefully();
            group.shutdownGracefully();
        }

    }

    @ChannelHandler.Sharable
    static class BadChannelHandler extends ChannelHandlerAdapter {

        @Override
        public void handlerAdded(ChannelHandlerContext ctx) throws Exception {
            TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS.sleep(10);
            throw new RuntimeException();
        }

    }

    static class NoopChannelHandler extends ChannelHandlerAdapter {
        @Override
        public void exceptionCaught(ChannelHandlerContext ctx, Throwable cause) {
            // NOOP
        }
    }
}
```
